## Evidence gaps

Detailed scene histories, albums beyond the starting three, independent 2026 reviews, international discovery, and annual candidate pools still require research. Release metadata does not establish musical quality; platform tags and promotional copy do not settle classification. Exact-day discrepancies are preserved rather than silently resolved.

Added 10 October 2026: independent review coverage is the largest remaining gap — only *Executing Nostalgia* has a located third-party review among the newly added titles. Core gothic rock eligibility for Kylmä Krypta and The Last Decade currently rests on artist and label framing rather than independent appraisal. The Bat-Cave page for *Omelas* was unreachable and should be rechecked. Corpus Delicti demonstrates why interview chatter is not release metadata: an October 2026 discussion of new songs preceded an album that had already shipped in November 2025.

